## Prerequisites

- Namespace/project access on Arvan
- One of:
  - Arvan panel + manifest deploy,
  - `kubectl` configured,
  - Arvan CLI (`arvan paas`) / Cloud Shell
- Helm v3 (for chart-based deployments)
- Values files:
  - `values.yaml` (non-secret)
  - `values.secret.yaml` (secret, not committed)

## Preflight (run before every install/upgrade)

```bash
bash .codex/skills/caas-arvan-kuber/scripts/verify-cluster.sh <namespace> [runner-serviceaccount]
bash .codex/skills/caas-arvan-kuber/scripts/render-helm.sh ./helm/<chart> <namespace> values.yaml values.secret.yaml rendered.yaml [values.<env>.yaml]
kubectl apply --dry-run=client -f rendered.yaml
```

## Install / Upgrade (Helm)

```bash
helm upgrade --install <release> ./helm/<chart> \
  -n <namespace> --create-namespace \
  -f values.yaml \
  -f values.<env>.yaml \
  -f values.secret.yaml \
  --wait --timeout 10m --rollback-on-failure
```

## Rollback

```bash
helm history <release> -n <namespace>
helm rollback <release> <revision> -n <namespace>
```

## Uninstall

```bash
helm uninstall <release> -n <namespace>
```

## Arvan safety requirements

1) Every container must declare resources.
- On Arvan targets, keep `requests == limits`.
- Include `ephemeral-storage` when required by policy.

2) Secret handling:
- never commit `values.secret.yaml`,
- never use `--set` for secret values,
- never print secrets in logs.

3) Scaling:
- HPA by default for stateless workloads only.
- Stateful/PVC-backed workloads: use manual replica/instance runbook.

4) Config mounts:
- mount secrets/configmaps into dedicated subdirectories to avoid shadowing existing files.

## Private registry pattern

Use `kubernetes.io/dockerconfigjson` and `imagePullSecrets` with two supported modes:

1) Helm-managed secret from `values.secret.yaml`
2) Existing secret reference (chart does not create/overwrite)

For GitLab Runner:

- ensure executor job pods render `image_pull_secrets`,
- pin helper image to a reachable registry path.

## Values layering (recommended)

Order:

1) `values.yaml`
2) `values.<env>.yaml` (optional, non-secret)
3) `values.secret.yaml` (last)

## Verify deployment

```bash
kubectl -n <namespace> get pods
kubectl -n <namespace> get svc,ingress
kubectl -n <namespace> describe pod <pod>
kubectl -n <namespace> logs <pod>
```

## Fast debug commands

```bash
helm get values <release> -n <namespace> -a
helm get manifest <release> -n <namespace> > release.rendered.yaml
kubectl -n <namespace> get events --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp
```

## RBAC identity debug note

If authorization failures look inconsistent, collect both namespace forms and principal identity before changing RBAC:

- alias namespace (human-friendly)
- canonical namespace (hash-prefixed when present)
- principal evaluated: `system:serviceaccount:<namespace>:<name>`

Use `references/arvan-rbac-namespace-facts.md` as the factual model.
